<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Mediomatrici</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Divodurum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of the Moselle valley whose chief town Divodurum became the city of Metz.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Mediomatrici held the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seille-moselle">Seille</a> valleys in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-lorraine">Lorraine</a>. Caesar notes that their territory once reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanic-peoples">Germanic peoples</a> such as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/triboci">Triboci</a> settled on its left bank.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of their rulers. Their territory lay on the trade routes linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saone">Saône</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a>, and their oppidum at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metz">Divodurum</a> controlled the Moselle crossing.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>They sent five thousand men to relieve <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alesia">Alesia</a> in 52 BCE. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metz">Divodurum</a> became a major town on the road from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a>, known in late antiquity as Mettis after the people, from which comes Metz, later capital of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/austrasia">Austrasia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/mediomatrici.jpg" alt="Mediomatrici" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: User:Feitscherg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Gallia_Tribes_Towns.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Divodurum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=mediomatrici" aria-label="Mediomatrici on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4765 540 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Mediomatrici lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5085 796h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5085 796h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day France. <a href="/atlas?year=-176&amp;focus=mediomatrici">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

